# newdoc id = GUM_conversation_lambada
# global.Entity = GRP-etype-infstat-salience-centering-minspan-link-identity
# meta::author = Santa Barbara Corpus of Spoken American English (ed. John W. Du Bois)
# meta::dateCollected = 2021-08-09
# meta::dateCreated = 2000-01-02
# meta::dateModified = 2000-01-02
# meta::genre = conversation
# meta::salientEntities = 1 (5*), 40 (5*), 17 (3*), 33 (3*), 39 (3), 53 (3*), 55 (3*), 34 (2*), 44 (2*), 76 (2), 4 (1*), 11 (1*), 54 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.linguistics.ucsb.edu/research/santa-barbara-corpus#SBC002
# meta::speakerCount = 4
# meta::summary1 = (human1) While discussing plans to go to a dance class in Bahia to learn lambada dancing, Miles tells his friends about an attractive woman he had seen dancing lewdly with a man there.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) A group of friends talk about going out and engaging in social dance, and Miles shares stories about the kinds of overt sensual behaviors he's seen at the club, to which most of his friends are initially fascinated and then put off when they realize how the story ends.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) Miles recounts some of his experiences dancing to friends Jamie and Harold, recounting in particular a time when a woman he went with did not want to dance and was approached by multiple men, and another time in which he saw an attractive woman dancing suggestively with a man in his fifties, and then later saw that woman talking and kissing another random guy.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) A man asks his friends, Harold and Miles, about going out to dance, but then Miles tells a story about when he went out a few weeks ago and saw a woman who was first dancing suggestively with a middle-aged man and then didn’t dance with him again and instead hooked up with other men at the club, and after this story they say that maybe they shouldn’t go dancing after all.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) Jamie is curious about going to a Lambada class Miles has been to and asks him what it's like, and the story he tells about the stupefying promiscuity he witnessed at a past class ends up convincing Jamie she shouldn't attend.
# meta::title = Lambada
