# newdoc id = GUM_conversation_retirement
# global.Entity = GRP-etype-infstat-salience-centering-minspan-link-identity
# meta::author = Santa Barbara Corpus of Spoken American English (ed. John W. Du Bois)
# meta::dateCollected = 2020-09-07
# meta::dateCreated = 2000-01-01
# meta::dateModified = 2000-01-01
# meta::genre = conversation
# meta::salientEntities = 5 (5*), 45 (5*), 58 (5*), 2 (4*), 21 (4), 3 (2*), 23 (2), 25 (2), 34 (2), 44 (2*), 46 (2), 69 (2), 1 (1*), 4 (1*), 12 (1), 26 (1), 62 (1), 65 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://www.linguistics.ucsb.edu/research/santa-barbara-corpus#SBC011
# meta::speakerCount = 3
# meta::summary1 = (human1) Friends discuss Sam's interest in retirement, whether or not some people they know who are involved in politics are political appointees, and growing basil.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) Sam and two other speakers briefly touch on numerous topics: Sam’s newfound interest in retirement, knowing Reg Barr, the behavior of a political appointee named Duvall and his association with Steitler, growing basil from seed, and smoking.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) Two friends discuss retirement plans as well as the political and business associations amongst various political appointees on a board, before discussing growing basil from seed, and then remarking on their smoking habits.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) Sam and her two friends talk about retirement and speaking to some people on the board who do not want to be known as political appointees before discussing herb growing, particularly of basil and oregano, and commenting on how they prefer to smoke their cigarettes.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) On a smoke break, two colleagues discuss their surprise that another colleague Sam is interested in retirement, as well as people they need to call, including a Doctor Duvall, who lied about not being a political appointee, and then Sam joins the conversation and the three of them discuss growing herbs, particularly basil.
