# meta::genre = speech
# meta::salientEntities = 56 (5*), 3 (4*), 82 (4*), 90 (4*), 29 (3*), 167 (3*), 1 (2*), 58 (2*), 59 (2*), 89 (2*), 92 (2*), 129 (2), 132 (2), 170 (2*), 8 (1), 10 (1), 12 (1*), 24 (1), 57 (1*), 63 (1), 64 (1), 130 (1), 139 (1), 165 (1), 166 (1), 169 (1*), 172 (1*), 175 (1), 188 (1), 190 (1)
# meta::sourceURL = https://dataverse.harvard.edu/dataset.xhtml?persistentId=doi:10.7910/DVN/0TJX8Y
# meta::speakerCount = 1
# meta::summary1 = (human1) In a 2011 speech to the UN General Assembly in the wake of the Arab Spring, Austria calls for action in the Arab world against violence and human rights violations, for the promotion of peace in the Middle East and the development of energy efficiency and renewable energy.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) In a 2011 speech at the UN, Austria urges the United Nations to take decisive action towards creating change in the Arab world and Middle East peace process for the sake of the current generation and future generations.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) In a speech to the United Nations, a representative of Austria makes an appeal to help humanitarian efforts in the Arab world, including fighting terrorism and oppressive governments, peace and mediation, and energy efficiency and nuclear safety.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) Around the time of the UN General Assembly, a representative of Austria gives a speech addressing geopolitical issues in Africa and the Middle East and the nuclear disaster in Fukushima, stressing the importance of Vienna as a hub for mediation and peace.
# meta::summary5 = (human5) With recent fights for human rights in the Middle East, Austria encourages dialogue and reforms for meaningful change rather than violence, as well as vocalizes support in providing humanitarian assistance and access to modern energy services.
# meta::title = Statement by H.E. Dr. Michael Spindelegger Vice-Chancellor and Federal Minister for European and International Affairs of the Republic of Austria at the 66th Session of the General Assembly of the United Nations
