# meta::summary1 = (human1) A minister in the New Zealand House of Representative announces the first case of the COVID-19 coronavirus in New Zealand and details efforts to conduct contact tracing and contain the outbreak through self-isolation, sending health staff to meet incoming flights at airports and preparing the public health system.
# meta::summary2 = (human2) On Friday, 28 February, New Zealand records its first reported case of COVID and details the government's response to contain the spread of the virus.
# meta::summary3 = (human3) This parliamentary statement announced the first confirmed case of COVID-19 in New Zealand, brought into the country by an individual who had arrived from Iran, and established the three protocols the government would take to contain the spread of the disease: border control, self-isolation, and good public health practices - like basic hygiene.
# meta::summary4 = (human4) On February 28, New Zealand announces its first recorded case of COVID-19 and emphasizes their tools of border controls, self-isolation, and good public health practices for protecting the health and safety of the wider public.
